-<p>Completeness: the six elements together are the whole defined scope. A Topic Maps revision whose identity can be checked (1), a Project Workspace that reads the unchanged project CTM with it (2), project work a reader can navigate and inspect in that Workspace (3), a public Inspector that is safe to expose (4), the regular Catalog package built reproducibly (5) and its verified deployment (6). What the scope needs and does not deliver are preconditions of the plan below: the user's admission of the Project Workspace to a served runtime, an independent security review, the decision to publish the archive and the approval of the production activation. Project management is not an element: this scope proposal and the integration review deliver no package.</p>
+<p>Completeness: the six elements together are the whole defined scope. A Topic Maps revision whose identity can be checked (1), a Project Workspace that reads the unchanged project CTM with it (2), project work a reader can navigate and inspect in that Workspace (3), a public Inspector that is safe to expose (4), the regular Catalog package built reproducibly (5) and its verified deployment (6). What the scope needs and does not deliver are preconditions of the plan below: an independent security review, the decision to publish the archive and the approval of the production activation. The Project Workspace is read, inspected and tested locally and is not admitted to the served regular Catalog within this scope: the Catalog's startup guard refuses it and stays; admitting it would be a separate decision of the user. Project management is not an element: this scope proposal and the integration review deliver no package.</p>
 <p>Overlap: 1 and 5 meet at the snapshot: 1 makes the revision and its manifest verifiable, 5 builds the package that serves it. 2 and 3 both concern the Project Workspace: 2 that it reads the unchanged project CTM with the revision and refuses what it cannot identify, 3 what the project work shows and how it is navigated, including the reading of the integration. 4 and 6 meet at exposure: 4 makes the views safe, 6 activates them. Package 5 builds the same regular Catalog on which the separate staging package of <code>tmd-deployment</code> was modelled; it neither changes that package nor its running service.</p>
